// ============================================================================
// TESTING WORKFLOW
// ============================================================================

/*
1. Start the application:
   mvn spring-boot:run

2. Test health check (no auth):
   GET http://localhost:8080/health

3. Get all games (no auth):
   GET http://localhost:8080/api/games

4. Get specific game details:
   GET http://localhost:8080/api/games/1

5. [REQUIRES AUTH TOKEN] Get game content:
   GET http://localhost:8080/api/games/1/play?limit=5
   + Add Authorization header with valid JWT

6. [REQUIRES AUTH TOKEN] Submit answers:
   POST http://localhost:8080/api/games/1/submit
   + Add Authorization header with valid JWT
   + Add request body with answers and timeSpent

7. [REQUIRES AUTH TOKEN] Check progress:
   GET http://localhost:8080/api/progress
   + Add Authorization header with valid JWT

8. [REQUIRES AUTH TOKEN] Check statistics:
   GET http://localhost:8080/api/progress/stats
   + Add Authorization header with valid JWT
*/

// ============================================================================
// HOW TO GET JWT TOKEN FOR TESTING
// ============================================================================

/*
Using Keycloak:

1. Start Keycloak:
   docker run -p 8180:8080 \
     -e KEYCLOAK_ADMIN=admin \
     -e KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=admin \
     quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:latest \
     start-dev

2. Get token:
   POST http://localhost:8180/auth/realms/gamified-learning/protocol/openid-connect/token

   Body (form-urlencoded):
   - grant_type: password
   - client_id: gamified-learning-api
   - client_secret: your-client-secret
   - username: test-user
   - password: test-password

3. Extract access_token from response
4. Use it in Authorization header: Bearer <access_token>

Alternative (for testing without Keycloak):
Generate a JWT at jwt.io with payload:
{
  "sub": "user-123",
  "name": "Test User",
  "iat": 1705756800,
  "exp": 9999999999
}
*/

